---
id: org.dxos.plugin.freeq
name: FreeqPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A Composer plugin that integrates freeq — an IRCv3-over-WebSocket chat service
that authenticates users via AT Protocol / Bluesky identities — as a live
channel backend for the DXOS Composer thread plugin. The plugin connects to a
freeq server over WebSocket, authenticates using the ATPROTO-CHALLENGE SASL
mechanism, joins an IRC channel, streams inbound messages in real time, and
sends outbound messages from the Composer composer. Messages are transient:
live messages are held in memory for the session and channel history is
backfilled from freeq's read-only REST API on join. A single WebSocket is
shared across every Composer channel that targets the same server and
identity.

The `FreeqChannel` schema, the shared `ConnectionManager` capability, and the
live `ChannelBackend` capability are implemented. Authenticated send is
validated against the freeq reference client but not yet confirmed against a
server that accepts app-password `pds-session` SASL tokens; v1 ships
read-capable, with guest (unauthenticated) channels supported end-to-end.

## Extensions

| Term   | URI                        |
|--------|----------------------------|
| `flow` | `org.dxos.mdl.flow@1.0`    |

## QA

Executable flows. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by flow and step number.

```mdl
flow QA-1: Join a guest channel and read backfilled history
  desc: |
    The plugin's only user-visible surface — plugin-thread renders a Channel whose
    `backend.config` is a FreeqChannel; freeq itself contributes no app graph action, no create
    operation, and no runtime operation of any kind (`grep` for `Operation.make` under
    `src/` returns nothing). Reaching this flow requires a Channel object whose backend config
    already points at a live freeq server, which today can only be constructed in code
    (`makeFreeqChannel`) — there is no navtree/UI path to attach one.
  actors: human
  covers: []
  status: blocked            # 2026-08-27; no operation exists to create or join a channel from the running app
  given:
    - plugin-freeq is enabled — it IS on by default (`FreeqPlugin.make()` unconditional in plugin-defs.tsx)
    - plugin-thread is enabled, since freeq only supplies a backend for its Channel object
    - a reachable freeq server and IRC channel with existing history (e.g. `wss://freeq.example`, `#general`)
    - a Channel object in the open space whose `backend.config` is a `FreeqChannel` pointing at
      that server/channel with no `handle` set (guest/read-only) — there is no in-app action to
      create this; it must be pre-seeded via `makeFreeqChannel` and `space.db.add` before the flow starts
  test:
    - name: Open the channel
      do: Click the freeq-backed Channel in the navtree.
      expect: the thread pane opens, the WebSocket connects (guest SASL), and the channel's REST-backfilled history renders as messages
      blocked: |
        No `invoke` exists — freeq contributes no operations, and connection/join is driven
        entirely by `ConnectionManager.acquire` inside `ChannelBackend`'s React lifecycle, not
        through anything the operation invoker can call.
    - name: Receive a live message
      do: From another IRC client, post a message to the same channel.
      expect: the message appears in the thread pane in real time, attributed to the sender's nick
      blocked: No operation surfaces the live WebSocket stream to the debug port; this can only be observed visually.
  after:
    - name: Close the channel
      do: Navigate away from the Channel plank.
      expect: the shared WebSocket connection is released once no open channel targets that server/identity pair
```
